#: a55d86e403b243268d8316b9e0e16a68 of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback:1
msgid "Report validation metrics to an Optuna trial and track the best value."
msgstr "Report validation metrics to an Optuna trial and track the best value."

#: faa4f5f3976c42e3a0e634ed7846fc4a of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback:3
msgid ""
"Supports pruning: sets the ``pruned`` flag and lets the training loop end"
" gracefully via ``should_stop`` (preserving resource cleanup in "
"``on_train_end`` / ``_finish``). The caller is expected to raise "
"``TrialPruned`` after ``run()`` returns."
msgstr ""
"Supports pruning: sets the ``pruned`` flag and lets the training loop end"
" gracefully via ``should_stop`` (preserving resource cleanup in "
"``on_train_end`` / ``_finish``). The caller is expected to raise "
"``TrialPruned`` after ``run()`` returns."

#: f6e2fb1c96404a4c9d2b2993dc89cd37 of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback:8
msgid ""
"Multi-stage safe: ``on_train_begin`` fires once per stage, so the per-"
"stage best/stop state is reset between stages while ``pruned`` stays "
"sticky (once any stage is pruned the whole trial is pruned). "
"``trial.report`` uses a monotonic counter rather than the per-stage "
"epoch, which restarts at 0 each stage and would otherwise make the step "
"regress across stages."
msgstr ""
"Multi-stage safe: ``on_train_begin`` fires once per stage, so the per-"
"stage best/stop state is reset between stages while ``pruned`` stays "
"sticky (once any stage is pruned the whole trial is pruned). "
"``trial.report`` uses a monotonic counter rather than the per-stage "
"epoch, which restarts at 0 each stage and would otherwise make the step "
"regress across stages."

#: 681a6cfaece34347a4824a0e6c1a9103 of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback.on_phase_end:1
msgid "Handle end-of-phase events: report validation metrics to Optuna."
msgstr "Handle end-of-phase events: report validation metrics to Optuna."

#: 956e0a45f4df4f3a8132de922f89fd8e of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback.on_phase_end:3
msgid "Reports the metric value to the trial and checks for pruning."
msgstr "Reports the metric value to the trial and checks for pruning."

#: 268060dd7f6143dd9b49541b85e38331 of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback.on_train_begin:1
msgid "Reset per-stage pruning state."
msgstr "Reset per-stage pruning state."

#: e34242b7b4a94af2849ac998782b8ce1 of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback.on_train_begin:3
msgid ""
"``on_train_begin`` fires once per stage in multi-stage trainers, so this "
"isolates each stage's best/stop tracking while leaving the sticky "
"``pruned`` untouched. For single-stage trainers this is a single no-op "
"reset of the constructor defaults."
msgstr ""
"``on_train_begin`` fires once per stage in multi-stage trainers, so this "
"isolates each stage's best/stop tracking while leaving the sticky "
"``pruned`` untouched. For single-stage trainers this is a single no-op "
"reset of the constructor defaults."

#: 7ebfbd382bde4929a8d331e119a07037 of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback.should_stop:1
msgid "Check whether the current stage should stop due to pruning."
msgstr "Check whether the current stage should stop due to pruning."

#: 7f3564996eae46989c0c01dc27bc75ad of
#: utils.optuna_utils.callback.OptunaTrialCallback.should_stop:3
msgid "True if the current stage has been pruned."
msgstr "True if the current stage has been pruned."

#: 3da077be3cf948748af75117ae905c7e of utils.case_analysis.base_analyzer:1
msgid "Base analyzer class for case analysis."
msgstr "Base analyzer class for case analysis."

#: bd4043031b9442f7b1a8225f3aba25e6 of utils.case_analysis.base_analyzer:3
msgid ""
"Minimal inference-only lifecycle: the analyzer is built from an archived "
"RunConfig plus a trained checkpoint, runs forward passes without an "
"optimizer or training loop, and hands extracted case data to an "
"injectable :class:`~utils.case_analysis.interfaces.CaseDataSink`."
msgstr ""
"Minimal inference-only lifecycle: the analyzer is built from an archived "
"RunConfig plus a trained checkpoint, runs forward passes without an "
"optimizer or training loop, and hands extracted case data to an "
"injectable :class:`~utils.case_analysis.interfaces.CaseDataSink`."

#: de0956ce72c34994ad3496c43c809acf of utils.case_analysis.base_analyzer:8
msgid ""
"Unlike the training path it does not subclass :class:`BaseTrainer`; "
"shared tensor/device helpers come from "
":class:`~utils.training.inference_ops.InferenceOpsMixin`."
msgstr ""
"Unlike the training path it does not subclass :class:`BaseTrainer`; "
